---
/*
  THE MEASURING DIAGRAM (section 73). Three hairline dimension lines on a
  plain garment silhouette, in the order the form asks: across the top for
  the shoulders, across the widest point for the chest, down the side for
  the length. Tailor's-diagram grammar — a line with two end ticks — in the
  site's one stroke weight, currentColor, no fill, no text (the written
  instructions beside it stay the source of truth in both languages, so the
  drawing never needs translating).

  IT IS OURS, NOT HIS: an invented visual on the one page where clarity
  beats style. Flagged `measureDiagram` in inventedCopy and counted by
  launch-check until the owner approves it; aria-hidden, because it repeats
  what the instructions already say.
*/
---

<svg
  class="measure-diagram"
  viewBox="0 0 260 300"
  aria-hidden="true"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="1.5"
>
  {/* the garment: a plain sleeveless torso, nobody's piece in particular */}
  <path d="M 34 52 C 60 44, 88 40, 106 38 C 114 46, 146 46, 154 38 C 172 40, 200 44, 226 52 L 218 96 L 206 90 L 208 272 L 52 272 L 54 90 L 42 96 Z" />

  {/* shoulders: across the top */}
  <g>
    <line x1="34" y1="24" x2="226" y2="24" />
    <line x1="34" y1="19" x2="34" y2="29" />
    <line x1="226" y1="19" x2="226" y2="29" />
  </g>

  {/* chest: across the widest point, under the arms */}
  <g>
    <line x1="54" y1="118" x2="206" y2="118" />
    <line x1="54" y1="113" x2="54" y2="123" />
    <line x1="206" y1="113" x2="206" y2="123" />
  </g>

  {/* length: from the base of the neck down to the hem */}
  <g>
    <line x1="244" y1="46" x2="244" y2="272" />
    <line x1="239" y1="46" x2="249" y2="46" />
    <line x1="239" y1="272" x2="249" y2="272" />
  </g>
</svg>
